  "story_id": "S089",
  "title": "Atxn1 and Cic converge on a thalamic synaptic reporter module",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Atxn1 perturbation generated a 187-gene 151 TH response with Dclk1 up, Lrrc7 down, Tecr up, Aldh1l2 up, Trim9 down, Ankrd55 up, and Grin2c down. The report identified Cic as the top non-Atxn1 151 TH signature neighbor, with Pearson r=0.543 across 17,259 genes and all 130 shared FDR genes having the same sign.",
  "biological_interpretation": "The Atxn1-loss-like adult thalamic state is strongly CIC-linked and nominates a compact mixed-direction reporter module rather than a generic ataxia-gene response.",
